course: dictionary
lesson: 12752
title: Duplication: copies and repeats
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Duplication is a noun. It can mean making an exact copy of something, or the copy itself. It can also mean doing the same work twice when once would be enough. In science, it means a part of a gene that is copied twice. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning.
explain: «The teacher made a duplication of the map for each group.» Here the duplication is the copy: every group gets an exact copy of the map. «We must avoid duplication, so Sam draws the map and Ana writes the story.» Here it means doing the same job twice, which wastes time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «avoid duplication» means do not do the same job twice, then «do not do the same job twice» should still make sense. It does, so you have chosen correctly.
fact: Duplication is a noun: a duplication, duplications. It can also be uncountable.
fact: «Duplication» can mean making an exact copy of something, or the copy itself.
fact: «Duplication of effort» means doing the same work twice when once would be enough.
fact: In computing, data duplication means the same file stored twice.
fact: In science, «gene duplication» means a part of a chromosome or gene that is copied twice, and it is one way living things change over time.
exercise: «The teacher made a duplication of the spelling test for each child.» What is the duplication here? | A spelling bee | A cancelled test | A new test with harder words | *An exact copy of the spelling test
exercise: «We must avoid duplication, so Sam draws the map and Ana writes the story.» What does avoid duplication mean? | Work faster than everyone else | Draw the map twice to be sure | Ask the teacher for more paper | *Do not do the same job twice
exercise: Kai says the scientist found «gene duplication» in the plant. What does it mean? | A test that checks plants | A gene that has been lost forever | *A part of a gene that is copied twice | A plant that grows in the dark
test: «Our computer saved the same photo twice, which is data duplication.» What is data duplication? | Taking a photo of the sky | Deleting a photo | *The same file stored twice | Sending a photo to a friend
test: «The two groups did the same sums, which was a duplication of effort.» What does duplication of effort mean? | Working very fast | Sharing the prize | Doing sums with a calculator | *Doing the same work twice when once would be enough
exam: In maths, what can duplication mean? | Dividing | Halving | *Doubling | Subtracting
